{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1452826-cloak-of-leaves-question","id":1452826,"title":"Cloak of Leaves Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-18T15:38:09-07:00","id":1452826,"title":"Cloak of Leaves Question","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> My next question regards the Cloak of Leaves Merit on page 111 of Changeling the Lost 2e. The Merit says: <br /> <br /> \u201cAnyone using a supernatural ability to cause damage or inflict physical Tilts upon the character suffers a penalty equal to his dots in this Merit. Supernatural abilities include Contracts, kith blessings, vampire Disciplines, mage spells, and any other innate ability used by a supernatural creature.\u201d<br /> <br /> So in the case of a Contract such as Helios\u2019 Judgment, does the penalty apply to the activation roll for the Contract? Or does it apply to each attack with the Contract (acting like a bonus to Defense)?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, does this penalty apply against other innate changeling abilities such as Hedgespinning and Oneiromancy?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T16:06:48-07:00","id":1452828,"title":"","content":"If the Activation roll is the same as the attack roll, yes, if not, no.<br /> <br /> I'll have to get back to you on Hedgespinnign and Oneiromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T05:34:00-07:00","id":1452939,"title":"","content":"I would say it works on attacks made with supernatural powers directly, but not on attacks made with weapons created by supernatural abilities. Because you're not using a supernatural ability on the target at that point, you're simply wielding an object that has a supernatural origin.<br /> <br /> So it would not work on attacks made with a Helios' Judgement javelin, nor on an attack with a weapon that was created using Oneiromancy or Hedgespinning.<br /> <br /> In theory, it should work on <i>direct </i>attacks (though there's no example of such a Shift in the table, but they should be possible) and Tilts made using Oneiromancy and Hedgespinning; however, you don't actually <i>know</i> what successes on a 'spinning roll are going to be used for when the character rolls the dice pool. Since they're really just rolling for a mundane skill and then fueling some successes into 'spinning.<br /> <br /> This is an unfortunate side effect of the way 'spinning is set up, along with the odd feeling of rolling a skill check, being told by the game system that your roll is a &quot;success&quot;, yet actually failing to do what you wanted to do because the mundane dimension of the roll you made is of no importance to you, the 'spinning was what it was all about and for.<br /> 'spinning as a distinct instant action with negative modifiers according to the difficulty of what you're trying to do would play better with merits such as this.<br /> <br /> You could let them roll Cloak of Leaves dots as a dice pool and subtract any successes from the attacker's successes the moment they declare they're 'spinning against them, but it's going to play enormously awkwardly, as you either first distribute all successes and then roll (in which case, 1 single success on the Cloak of Leaves will always stop the attack/Tilt since it'll make them 1 success short of the effect they're trying to do) or you first declare your targets, then those targets roll, then you subtract successes, then you distribute successes which... is also super awkward and allows the attacker to just change their action or funnel more successes to you (if they can) to get the same result anyway, foregoing some fringe benefit instead.<br /> I don't think the current system can be made to play nicely with merits or abilities such as the one in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}